            <ArticleTitle>First experience with a new analgesic drug: buprenorphine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>134-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Buprenorphine, a new analgesic drug, was used for treatment of immediate postoperative pain in a group of 30 patients. A standard dose of 4 mug/kg was given IM. Onset of action occurred 10 to 20 min. later; pain relief was very good to good in 73%, fairly good in 23% and insufficient in 3%. Duration of action was very long (Mean + SEM: 360 +/- 32 min.) Side effects were few.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
